  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This theoretical paper demonstrates that indefinite metamaterials can exhibit effective metric signature transitions, mimicking phenomena from quantum gravity and Bose-Einstein condensates. Key findings include the prediction that such transitions create a Minkowski space-time and a large number of particles, with numerical calculations showing significant photon emission during light-induced phase transitions in gallium-based metamaterials. The authors acknowledge limitations such as metamaterial losses limiting particle creation and the use of a 'sudden change' approximation for dispersion law.",
